{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Who has counted the dust of Jacob.</b> Who can count the dust-particles of Jacob — these are the children, who are small; that is, there are also among them young children who are not included in the count, for Israel were counted only from twenty years and upward. It follows that the dust of Jacob is the little ones, who outnumber the adults many times over. And if the adults sinned, the little ones did not sin; therefore he does not desire their curse." "<b>And the number of the fourth part of Israel.</b> One quarter of their four banners, as it is written: ״אפס קצהו תראה״ etc." "<b>Let my soul die the death of the upright.</b> He saw in his astrology that he was destined to fall by the sword."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:26.516399627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}